Shanling's hooks for BlueZ 5.88, for the stock base alone (docs/bluez.md#bases): what stock's bluetoothd does
for demo and Shanling's libbtctl.so, written anew against upstream's source from docs/bluetoothd.md's
description of it, never from Shanling's code. Applied by tools/thirdparty.py's build_bluez after vamp.patch
when BLUEZ_BASE is 'stock'; a base whose UI talks to org.bluez itself leaves this whole patch out. Licensed as
the code it changes, GPL-2.0-or-later. Ported from feat/bt-browse's patch for 5.66 (docs/bluez.md, Shanling's
changes), less its AVRCP browsing for coda-rc, which is a feature of its own:

- src/main.c: bluez_main() at start (shanling.bluez); Makefile.am links libbtctl.so and what it leans on.
- profiles/audio/avrcp.c: GetPlayStatus and GetElementAttributes from libbtctl's g_play_status and
  g_track_meta; demo's notifications to the target session (g_avrcp_event_fun, g_hci_session); Shanling's
  set of notification events; the phone's track to the receiver page (PlayInfoChange 0x104).
- profiles/audio/avdtp.c, a2dp.c: the receiver page told of a phone's stream starting and suspending; the
  local endpoints ordered by g_high_priority_lcodec (the Quality page's codec); the endpoint a headset
  configured registered.
- avctp.c, avdtp.c, policy.c: SyncLink's reads of g_synclink_mode.
- profiles/shanling: the SyncLink SDP record (0xcc0c, RFCOMM 28) Shanling's phone app finds.
- src/adapter.c: g_hci_session cleared at a disconnection.

